---
# A conservative set: the checks that find bugs (bugprone-*), wasted work (performance-*), and a few
# modernize, readability and misc checks that agree with the existing style. tools/run_clang_tidy.py runs
# it over src/ and fails on findings not in its baseline (CONTRIBUTING.md).
#
# Left out, and why:
# - bugprone-easily-swappable-parameters: math code takes several floats or vectors in a row by design.
# - bugprone-signed-bitwise: flags and bit fields are built from int constants (Windows, Vulkan, the
#   game's own fields); the operands are never negative.
# - bugprone-multi-level-implicit-pointer-conversion, performance-no-int-to-ptr: the hooks read and patch
#   the game's memory through addresses and void pointers on purpose.
# - bugprone-throwing-static-initialization: file-scope containers in the layer; an allocation failure
#   while the DLL loads is not something it could recover from anyway.
# - misc-misplaced-const: Vulkan handles and function pointers are typedefs of pointers, so `const
#   VkDevice` is the intended const pointer.
# - performance-enum-size: the size of an enum is not where the layer's time or memory goes.
# - bugprone-implicit-widening-of-multiplication-result: index and size arithmetic on small ints, kept
#   readable.
# - bugprone-invalid-enum-default-initialization: the OpenXR, Vulkan and Direct3D info structs are
#   value-initialized (`{}`) and then filled; their C enums have no zero value.
# Also not enabled: the clang-analyzer-* checks (the path-sensitive analyzer, a much slower pass not tried
# on this code yet), the cppcoreguidelines-*, hicpp-* and other style sets, and the rest of modernize-* and
# readability-* (style the code does not follow; clang-format handles layout).
Checks: >
  -*,
  bugprone-*,
  performance-*,
  misc-redundant-expression,
  modernize-use-override,
  modernize-use-nullptr,
  modernize-redundant-void-arg,
  modernize-use-bool-literals,
  modernize-deprecated-headers,
  readability-misleading-indentation,
  readability-duplicate-include,
  readability-misplaced-array-index,
  readability-redundant-string-cstr,
  readability-delete-null-pointer,
  readability-static-accessed-through-instance,
  readability-string-compare,
  readability-container-size-empty,
  readability-redundant-smartptr-get,
  readability-inconsistent-declaration-parameter-name,
  -bugprone-easily-swappable-parameters,
  -bugprone-signed-bitwise,
  -bugprone-multi-level-implicit-pointer-conversion,
  -bugprone-throwing-static-initialization,
  -bugprone-implicit-widening-of-multiplication-result,
  -bugprone-invalid-enum-default-initialization,
  -performance-no-int-to-ptr,
  -performance-enum-size
WarningsAsErrors: ''
HeaderFilterRegex: '.*[/\\]src[/\\].*'
...
